    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "claude-sonnet-5"
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=Source material:\n{{ $json.article_text }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "system": "You extract distinct claims or ideas from source material for a content drafting pipeline. For each claim, identify the exact source span, a short quote or line, it came from. Respond with a JSON object containing a claims array; each entry has a text field and a source_span field. Return only JSON, no prose, no markdown code fences.",
          "maxTokens": 1500
        }
      },
      "id": "bb06dfe0-c9ce-4948-b047-a06cb3b04449",
      "name": "Extract And Trace Claims",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.anthropic",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        448,
        0
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "anthropicApi": {
          "id": null,
          "name": "Gateway credits",
          "__aiGatewayManaged": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "var item = $input.first().json;\nvar raw = \"\";\nif (typeof item.content === \"string\") { raw = item.content; }\nelse if (Array.isArray(item.content)) { var t = item.content.find(function(p){ return p && p.type === \"text\"; }); raw = t ? t.text : JSON.stringify(item.content); }\nelse if (typeof item.text === \"string\") { raw = item.text; }\nelse if (typeof item.output === \"string\") { raw = item.output; }\nelse { raw = JSON.stringify(item); }\nraw = raw.trim().replace(/^```json/i, \"\").replace(/^```/, \"\").replace(/```$/, \"\").trim();\nvar parsed;\ntry { parsed = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) { parsed = { claims: [] }; }\nvar submission = $(\"Prepare Submission\").first().json;\nvar out = Object.assign({}, submission, { claims: parsed.claims || [] });\nreturn [{ json: out }];"
      },
      "id": "f6688347-06c6-47a0-b50f-d8f51ea704bc",
      "name": "Parse Claims And Merge Context",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        672,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "claude-sonnet-5"
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=Claims to check:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.claims) }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "system": "You check claims against a creator archive and voice profile. Flag any claim that repeats a topic, company, or specific fact from a past post, not phrases the creator repeats on purpose. Also score how well a draft made from these claims would fit the creator voice, from zero to one hundred. Voice profile - structural template observed across this creator's LinkedIn posts: (1) an opening paragraph stating the news with two or three concrete numbers pulled directly from the source, often starting with the phrase A major; (2) a second paragraph explaining why it matters, often opening with By, For [company] this is a strategic move to, or This development is a significant milestone for; (3) a forward-looking, hedged paragraph, often ending with the phrase could serve as a blueprint for; (4) a closing line that is always a direct binary engagement question in the form Do you think A, or B. Tone is third-person analyst register, no first-person opinions stated directly, numbers-heavy, no emojis, no slang. Do not flag the recurring structural phrases above as repetition, since they are intentional voice. Only flag repeated topics or specific claims, such as the same company or the same event, as duplicates. Respond with a JSON object containing a claims array, each with text and repeated_on fields, a voice_score number, and a flags array of short strings. Return only JSON, no prose, no markdown code fences.",
          "maxTokens": 1000
        }
      },
      "id": "14e097c6-a98d-42bf-9c58-2bbf70a5e8e7",
      "name": "Archive And Voice Check",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.anthropic",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        880,
        0
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "anthropicApi": {
          "id": null,
          "name": "Gateway credits",
          "__aiGatewayManaged": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "var item = $input.first().json;\nvar raw = \"\";\nif (typeof item.content === \"string\") { raw = item.content; }\nelse if (Array.isArray(item.content)) { var t = item.content.find(function(p){ return p && p.type === \"text\"; }); raw = t ? t.text : JSON.stringify(item.content); }\nelse if (typeof item.text === \"string\") { raw = item.text; }\nelse if (typeof item.output === \"string\") { raw = item.output; }\nelse { raw = JSON.stringify(item); }\nraw = raw.trim().replace(/^```json/i, \"\").replace(/^```/, \"\").replace(/```$/, \"\").trim();\nvar parsed;\ntry { parsed = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) { parsed = {}; }\nvar prior = $(\"Parse Claims And Merge Context\").first().json;\nvar out = Object.assign({}, prior, { claims: parsed.claims || prior.claims, voice_score: parsed.voice_score || 0, flags: parsed.flags || [] });\nreturn [{ json: out }];"
      },
